{"comment_text": {"ja78:0.1": "", "ja78:0.2": "", "ja78:0.3": "", "ja78:0.4": "", "ja78:1.1": "A rich man was so miserly that Sakka took on his form, crippled though it was, to open the miser’s vaults for the people. The king is asked to adjudicate his case, but cannot tell which is which. ", "ja78:1.2": "", "ja78:1.3": "", "ja78:1.4": "The rich man was named after the Ilish herring (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>illisa</i>). This is still popular for eating in modern times, and as a result is threatened by overfishing, pollution, and global warming. | The commentary repeatedly calls him “miserly” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>macchariya</i>), suggesting that his name arose as a play on “fish” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>maccha</i>). His misadventures, in fact, were sparked by seeing a man eating rotten fish (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>pūtimacchaka</i>). ", "ja78:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja78:0.1": "<article id='ja78'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja78:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja78:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja78:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja78:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja78:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja78:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja78:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja78:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja78:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja78:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja78:0.3": "Varuṇavagga ", "ja78:0.4": "8. Illisajātaka ", "ja78:1.1": "“Ubho khañjā ubho kuṇī, ", "ja78:1.2": "ubho visamacakkhukā; ", "ja78:1.3": "Ubhinnaṁ piḷakā jātā, ", "ja78:1.4": "nāhaṁ passāmi illisan”ti. ", "ja78:2.1": "Illisajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja78:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 78 ", "ja78:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja78:0.3": "The Warding Tree ", "ja78:0.4": "Herring, the Miser: a past life story ", "ja78:1.1": "Both are lame, both crippled, ", "ja78:1.2": "both cross-eyed, ", "ja78:1.3": "and both covered in warts: ", "ja78:1.4": "I see not which is Herring. ", "ja78:2.1": ""}, "variant_text": {"ja78:0.1": "", "ja78:0.2": "", "ja78:0.3": "", "ja78:0.4": "", "ja78:1.1": "", "ja78:1.2": "", "ja78:1.3": "", "ja78:1.4": "", "ja78:2.1": "Illisajātakaṁ → illīsajātakaṁ (sya1ed, sya2ed, pts-vp-pli1) "}, "reference_text": {"ja78:0.1": "", "ja78:0.2": "", "ja78:0.3": "", "ja78:0.4": "", "ja78:1.1": "dr27.26, ms22J_172, msdiv78, pts-vp-pli1.353", "ja78:1.2": "", "ja78:1.3": "", "ja78:1.4": "", "ja78:2.1": "ms22J_173"}, "keys_order": ["ja78:0.1", "ja78:0.2", "ja78:0.3", "ja78:0.4", "ja78:1.1", "ja78:1.2", "ja78:1.3", "ja78:1.4", "ja78:2.1"]}